{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337769-viva-la-revoluci\u00f3n-help-with-a-character-on-realm","id":1337769,"title":"Viva la revoluci\u00f3n! - Help with a Character on Realm.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-24T22:46:20-07:00","id":1337769,"title":"Viva la revoluci\u00f3n! - Help with a Character on Realm.","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> First post here - although I have been following a lot of discussions since 2016, knowing more and more about this wonderful universe that is today, my favorite setting. <br /> <br /> I have a character concept that, well, I here to ask your help to develop it further. The basics:<br /> <br /> - Caste Eclipse or Night. I am still undecided with the Caste, being Eclipse the first option. Night Caste became an option because of Anima powers. I can give up if I can get an artifact that assign the keyword mute to certain charms. <br /> <br /> - Supernal, I'll go with Socialize. Fav/Caste I'll go with Bureaucracy, Occult ( for Sorcery), Martial Arts ( maybe Black Claw Style ) and Presence. <br /> <br /> The central idea is for the character to lead a criminal organization within the Realm, and use this organization against it. I wish you could help me with build suggestions and motivations for the character. <br /> <br /> What a revolutionary solar Exalted, living and working within the Realm would be like? <br /> <br /> I don't speak English ( usually I just read, rarely I writte something), so sorry for any problems. I hope I made me clear. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25210-heavenly-devil","name":"Heavenly Devil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T07:18:55-07:00","id":1337807,"title":"","content":"Well for one, you probably want to be a Night Caste. Night Castes can suppress their animas and treat all peripheral essence use as personal essence use for 2 motes. When surrounded by Immaculates, that will probably help tons. I don't know of any artifacts that add the mute keyword.<br /> <br /> You're going to want high manipulation.<br /> <br /> As far as what your character is going to be like? Ultra stealthy. Very paranoid. Anyone who finds out about your character being a Solar may turn on you. <br /> <br /> As far as starting charms, you don't want to be too broad. I'd probably get a couple dodge charms, a bunch of stealth, and then maybe a bureaucracy charm or two. You don't want to spread yourself too thing at the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T08:23:54-07:00","id":1337813,"title":"","content":"Many Larceny and Socialize Charms luckily already have the Mute keyword, so choosing Eclipse isn't <i>necessarily</i> a decision to shoot yourself in the foot (which is good, because being able to wrest supernaturally-binding promises from people is crazy awesome).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T10:49:17-07:00","id":1337827,"title":"","content":"My first piece of advice and/or question is, what are the other PCs in the game? Because that's a very important step - making sure your PC will align with them in a fun way. Is everyone else in the game on board with staying on the Blessed Isle and taking down the Realm from within? And is everyone okay with being subtle and covert about it? Because if either of those things <i>aren't</i> true, then either you or one of the other PCs might end up not having fun. Have you talked to your fellow players about what they want to play? Assuming you have, and that your concept works with theirs, here's some other advice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavenly Devil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337769-viva-la-revoluci\u00f3n-help-with-a-character-on-realm#post1337769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Caste Eclipse or Night. I am still undecided with the Caste, being Eclipse the first option. Night Caste became an option because of Anima powers. I can give up if I can get an artifact that assign the keyword mute to certain charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are strong choices for this character type. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> notes, a lot of the charms you're likely to be using already have Mute, so the Night's anima power to apply the Mute keyword is a bit less necessary. However, the other Night Caste powers (ignoring penalties to stealth and concealing your identity at bonfire/iconic) are still very nice. Of course, as TheCountAlucard also correctly notes, the Eclipse Caste oath-binding power is <i>also </i>very nice. The diplomatic immunity power could come up if you're dealing with gods who might otherwise rat you out to the Wyld Hunt, and the ability to learn spirit charms is always pretty sweet. I'd suggest, to make this decision, that you consider what <i>approach</i> will most define your character. Is she fundamentally sneaky, the sort of person who will use stealth, lies, and deceit preferentially, even when she doesn't have to? If that's the case, go with Night Caste. Or is she a more open, honest person, who <i>wants</i> to bargain fairly and get everyone to agree, but is forced by circumstances to be covert? Then go with Eclipse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavenly Devil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Supernal, I'll go with Socialize. Fav/Caste I'll go with Bureaucracy, Occult ( for Sorcery), Martial Arts ( maybe Black Claw Style ) and Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Socialize is a good choice for your Supernal, for sure. I would strongly suggest the &quot;persona&quot; charms within Socialize (starting with Heart-Eclipsing Shroud). They will allow you to create multiple personas, other personalities with different Intimacies and personalities from your base character. With more of the charms down the line, you can start giving them their own sets of Abilities and even charms, different from your main character. The base ability to create multiple personas is very useful when you'll be facing Dragon-Blooded, who have their own supernatural abilities to determine people's real Intimacies and intentions. A persona will allow you to conceal that extremely effectively, since while you're in the persona, you &quot;really&quot; have the Intimacies and such that you've built for it, and your &quot;base&quot; Intimacies are totally suppressed.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest having at least two personas, in addition to your base character. The first persona would be the &quot;leader of a criminal syndicate&quot; one, and have Intimacies related to just being a typical criminal, nothing specifically about hating the Realm or wanting it destroyed. The second would be a fairly innocuous &quot;respectable member of society&quot;, a merchant or otherwise reasonably well-off commoner. The idea would be to use the &quot;leader of a criminal syndicate&quot; persona for almost all your actual actions to control the criminal organization, and definitely to be in it whenever someone who might be a Dragon-Blood comes snooping around. That way, if they covertly read your Intimacies, they'll detect a criminal, but a &quot;normal&quot; one, not a Realm-hating threat. That could buy you a lot of time, since the Realm has a lot of things on its plate right now, and probably won't spend as many resources taking down a normal crime syndicate compared to one devoted to destabilizing the whole empire. The other persona, the innocuous one, is what you use to go out in public with, in order to avoid the possibility of random Dragon-Blooded reading incriminating Intimacies off you. It also gives you a nice place to &quot;retreat&quot; to, if your other personas or base personality are revealed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavenly Devil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The central idea is for the character to lead a criminal organization within the Realm, and use this organization against it. I wish you could help me with build suggestions and motivations for the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the Socialize persona charms I already mentioned, I'd also suggest picking up the following charms from Larceny:<ul><li>Seasoned Criminal Method, which is a generally good charm to have when dealing with the underworld.</li> <li>Spurious Presence and Preying on Uncertainty Approach, both good for being places other people don't want you to be.</li> <li>Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise, for creating really good disguises (use this one to make your personas look different from one another).</li> </ul>In addition to charms, you'll also want some merits. In particular, Followers is probably the best merit to represent control over a criminal organization. The number of dots you put in will depend on how large the organization is. Remember, you don't need to buy dots to represent <i>every </i>person influenced by the gang, just the people who actually recognize and accept you as the leader. If you take 3 dots, you have a hundred people who follow you personally, but that might mean there are ten times that many who are members of the gang, but who don't know who you are, and instead report to one of your followers. Represent this larger peripheral group with the Contacts and Influence merits. You might also want to take a Retainer or two, to represent particularly competent lieutenants. Besides all that, definitely consider buying Resources, because running an operation like this will take money, for things like bribes, buying assassinations, and other nefarious activities.<br /> <br /> <br /> For motivation, I think there's three broad categories that your character could fall into: <i>Anger</i>, <i>resentment</i>, and <i>idealism</i>.<br /> <br /> Anger is the simplest - you or people you're close to have been hurt by the Realm, and you want revenge. There's an awful lot of potential things in this category - the Realm harms a <i>lot</i> of people. One classic example would be: you were a member of a society conquered by the Realm, or an existing satrapy that rebelled. In the process of conquering/suppressing the rebellion, the Realm captured you and your family, and you were sold into slavery on the Blessed Isle. Another one could be: you belonged to a village of peasants on the Isle who were dispossessed and stripped of their citizenship, unjustly. The advantage of picking this type of motivation is that it's quite simple, and easy to sympathize with. You'll have a natural recruitment tool - just tell your story to people who've been similarly hurt, and explain what you're doing. You'll probably get a lot of people who sign up just based on that.<br /> <br /> Resentment is a bit more complex - you <i>believe</i> you've been hurt by the Realm, though an outside observer might not agree. But you think you've been denied something you deserve. This motivation is more likely to come from someone internal to the Realm - a Dynast chaffing because she was &quot;born to rule&quot; but never got the chance because she didn't Exalt as a Dragon-Blood, for example, or the child of a wealthy patrician family, objecting to the fact that the Dragon-Bloods and their immediate relatives have all the political power. This sort of motivation is perhaps a bit less easy to be sympathetic to, but it has its advantages too. It's a lot easier to justify useful traits like Contacts among the Dynasty or similar social stuff that a slave or a peasant just couldn't start with, for one thing. It can also lead to a more complex and interesting goal - rather than just &quot;tear down the Realm&quot;, you could have a goal more along the lines of &quot;<i>reform</i> the Realm into something more fair/beneficial to me&quot;. <br /> <br /> Idealism is the most abstract motivation. You're not trying to bring down the Realm because it hurt you or didn't help you enough, you're just doing it because it's the right thing to do - you've recognized the injustice and cruelty built into the fabric of the Realm, and decided that it has to go. This sort of motivation can support someone from practically anywhere in Creation, since the Realm touches most of it, and even where it doesn't directly control or influence things, stories of it have penetrated. Idealism is also useful for making allies - you can join with characters who are angry or resentful of the Realm, of course, but lacking the anger and urge to hurt back might make it plausible to join forces with other idealists as well. For example, someone who resents the Dragon-Bloods might have difficulty making friends with an Outcaste who thinks the Dynasty is unfair and wants power distributed to more Dragon-Bloods in general, whereas an idealist might be willing to work with them for at least a little while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T12:28:43-07:00","id":1337837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337769-viva-la-revoluci\u00f3n-help-with-a-character-on-realm?p=1337827#post1337827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The diplomatic immunity power could come up if you're dealing with gods who might otherwise rat you out to the Wyld Hunt,</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll stop them from stabbing you, I don't think it'll stop them informing on you later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> concealing your identity at bonfire/iconic </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you're iconic as an Eclipse, you're going to be in deep, deep ****. With a Night, you can fight at almost-peak capacity without flaring at all, or fight at peak capacity and give the game away that there's a Solar, but there's a good chance they won't know who that Solars is. (Though it's not quite as good as it looks, because your caste-mark is quite likely glowing before and after you reach Bonfire.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I think Kelly's got a lot of good suggestions. The fake intimacies could be especially useful against Dragonblood investigators.<br /> <br /> <br /> One other thing you may want to consider is trying to acquire some kind of jade artefact. Doesn't have to be anything impressive. But a Dragonblood persona could be really useful, if people start wondering how you're so good at what you do. If you get Perfect Mirror, you can even do a few supernatural effects, like breathing smoke or having a wind around you, to make it especially convincing.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-25-2019, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T12:42:49-07:00","id":1337840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337769-viva-la-revoluci\u00f3n-help-with-a-character-on-realm?p=1337837#post1337837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'll stop them from stabbing you, I don't think it'll stop them informing on you later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends - the anima effects specifies that creatures affected by it &quot;must observe the local rules of hospitality.&quot; In at least some cultures, such rules probably include, if not total prevention of betraying your guests, at least some kind of &quot;grace period&quot; where you're not allowed to do so. And with high Socialize, you should be able to figure out the limitations of such rules of hospitality! Not to mention, if you can get them to swear oaths to not betray you, you've got them pretty good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing you may want to consider is trying to acquire some kind of jade artefact. Doesn't have to be anything impressive. But a Dragonblood persona could be really useful, if people start wondering how you're so good at what you do. If you get Perfect Mirror, you can even do a few supernatural effects, like breathing smoke or having a wind around you, to make it especially convincing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely agreed here. Perfect Mirror's an Essence 2 charm, so you'll have to wait a little bit to grab it, but it's probably worthwhile to start claiming your criminal leader persona is a Dragon-Blood right away anyway, to start establishing that idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T15:47:19-07:00","id":1337863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337769-viva-la-revoluci\u00f3n-help-with-a-character-on-realm?p=1337827#post1337827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Socialize is a good choice for your Supernal, for sure. I would strongly suggest the &amp;quot;persona&amp;quot; charms within Socialize (starting with Heart-Eclipsing Shroud). They will allow you to create multiple personas, other personalities with different Intimacies and personalities from your base character. With more of the charms down the line, you can start giving them their own sets of Abilities and even charms, different from your main character. The base ability to create multiple personas is very useful when you'll be facing Dragon-Blooded, who have their own supernatural abilities to determine people's real Intimacies and intentions. A persona will allow you to conceal that extremely effectively, since while you're in the persona, you &amp;quot;really&amp;quot; have the Intimacies and such that you've built for it, and your &amp;quot;base&amp;quot; Intimacies are totally suppressed.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest having at least two personas, in addition to your base character. The first persona would be the &amp;quot;leader of a criminal syndicate&amp;quot; one, and have Intimacies related to just being a typical criminal, <b>nothing specifically about hating the Realm or wanting it destroyed</b>. The second would be a fairly innocuous &amp;quot;respectable member of society&amp;quot;, a merchant or otherwise reasonably well-off commoner. The idea would be to use the &amp;quot;leader of a criminal syndicate&amp;quot; persona for almost all your actual actions to control the criminal organization, and definitely to be in it whenever someone who might be a Dragon-Blood comes snooping around. That way, if they covertly read your Intimacies, they'll detect a criminal, but a &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; one, not a Realm-hating threat. That could buy you a lot of time, since the Realm has a lot of things on its plate right now, and probably won't spend as many resources taking down a normal crime syndicate compared to one devoted to destabilizing the whole empire. The other persona, the innocuous one, is what you use to go out in public with, in order to avoid the possibility of random Dragon-Blooded reading incriminating Intimacies off you. It also gives you a nice place to &amp;quot;retreat&amp;quot; to, if your other personas or base personality are revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>How, exactly, does that play?<br /> <br /> Whilst in your criminal Persona, you don't have an Intimacy to topple the Realm... because you don't WANT to topple the Realm. Do you just play that as leading upto a great &quot;Just As Planned&quot; moment or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}